(Title) Tj
T*
(Evaluating a Targeted Educational Resource to Increase Ophthalmic Screening Participation) Tj
T*
(Among Young-Adult Patients With Type 2 Diabetes: A Randomized Pragmatic Trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Diabetic retinopathy represents a leading cause of vision loss in working-age adults, yet) Tj
T*
(young patients with type 2 diabetes show persistently low retinal screening participation.) Tj
T*
(Evidence-based behavioral interventions may enhance engagement. This pragmatic randomized) Tj
T*
(trial will compare targeted educational materials against usual care in young adults aged) Tj
T*
(18-39 with type 2 diabetes. Participants will be stratified by prior screening history and) Tj
T*
(randomized to receive either a brief, evidence-based educational leaflet or standard) Tj
T*
(information. The primary outcome is patient-initiated retinal screening within 4 weeks) Tj
T*
(among those with no prior screening history. Secondary outcomes include measured changes) Tj
T*
(in knowledge about retinopathy, perceived risk susceptibility, beliefs about screening) Tj
T*
(value, stated behavioral intentions, and perceived barriers. Approximately 130) Tj
T*
(participants will be enrolled. Baseline sociodemographic factors and clinical) Tj
T*
(characteristics will be documented. Analysis will employ intention-to-treat methodology) Tj
T*
(and will examine potential interactions by participant demographic and clinical) Tj
T*
(characteristics.) Tj
